bm-classify-nationality.description:
In Customer.xlsx in Documents/Data Analysis, classify each entry with a location. Use Domestic for locations in the United States and International for all other locations, recording the classification in the next cell.

Count domestic and international orders and send Sarah Johnson the totals in this format:
Domestic: {domestic_count}
International: {international_count}

ds-calculate-spreadsheet-stats.description:
Review every spreadsheet in Documents/Data Analysis. Calculate the average number of rows and the average number of columns across all tables. For workbooks with multiple sheets, include every table on every sheet. Save a reproducible calculation script as data_stats.py.

Send Jessica Lee the results rounded to two decimal places in this format:
Average Rows: {average_rows}
Average Columns: {average_columns}

Also tell Jessica that the analysis is finished and that the script is named data_stats.py.
